<title>SWITZERLAND: LGT 1996 net jumps 35 pct, dividend raised.</title>
<headline>LGT 1996 net jumps 35 pct, dividend raised.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calender 1996 vs 1995:</p>
<p>				   (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net profit	     174.1	     vs 128.9</p>
<p> Gross earnings		 679.3	     vs 576.9</p>
<p> Ordinary pre-tax profit    204.8	     vs 159.7</p>
<p>Dividend per certificate,</p>
<p> share, Sfr		     22		  vs 20</p>
<p>Earnings per certificate</p>
<p> share, Sfr		     57.75	     vs 43.49</p>
<p> Net assets per share, sfr  391.01	    vs 360.67</p>
<p> Return on Equity (ROE),pct 14.7		vs 11.9</p>
<p>NOTE - Private bank and fund manager Liechtenstein Global Trust AG (LGT) said the first two months of 1997 had been very successful and LGT expects a positive development of business in the entire year, barring unexpected market influences.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
